ARTICLE I. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION

Section 1.01. Defined Terms

For purposes of this License, the following terms shall have the meanings specified below:

(a) “Licensor” means mzyhot or any other person or legal entity possessing sufficient rights in particular Covered Materials to distribute such materials pursuant to this License.

(b) “Licensee” means any natural person or legal entity exercising, or seeking to exercise, rights granted under this License.

(c) “Covered Materials” means original, copyrightable source code, executable code, scripts, documentation, and other materials specifically developed for the Gluon project, to the extent such materials are owned or lawfully licensable by the applicable Licensor and expressly designated as governed by this License.

(d) “Third-Party Materials” means all software, source code, executable code, libraries, frameworks, dependencies, documentation, and other materials not expressly designated as Covered Materials by a person possessing the legal authority to make such designation.

(e) “CodeWeavers” means CodeWeavers, Inc., together with its successors, parent entities, subsidiaries, and entities directly or indirectly controlled by, controlling, or under common control with CodeWeavers, Inc.

(f) “Excluded Person” means any person or entity described in Article III.

(g) “Covered Rights” means the rights expressly granted under Article II.

(h) “Circumvention Arrangement” means any agreement, agency relationship, contractual undertaking, coordinated activity, or other demonstrable arrangement entered into for the purpose of enabling an Excluded Person to exercise Covered Rights that such Excluded Person is prohibited from exercising directly.

(i) “Derivative Work” means a work based upon one or more preexisting works that constitutes a derivative work under applicable copyright law.

(j) “Distribution” means making copies of Covered Materials available to another person or entity, whether commercially or noncommercially, including by sale, transfer, publication, or electronic transmission.

Section 1.02. Interpretation

Headings are included solely for convenience and shall not affect interpretation.

The terms “including” and “includes” shall be construed without limitation.

References to a person include legal entities where the context permits.

No provision shall be interpreted as granting rights that the applicable Licensor lacks authority to grant.

