ARTICLE III. EXCLUDED PERSONS AND ENTITIES

Section 3.01. Express Exclusion of CodeWeavers

NOTWITHSTANDING ANY PROVISION TO THE CONTRARY, NO LICENSE, AUTHORIZATION, OR PERMISSION IS GRANTED UNDER THIS LICENSE TO CODEWEAVERS OR ANY OTHER EXCLUDED PERSON.

The exclusion established by this Article constitutes an express limitation upon the persons eligible to receive and exercise Covered Rights.

Section 3.02. Categories of Excluded Persons

The following shall constitute Excluded Persons:

(a) CodeWeavers. CodeWeavers, as defined in Section 1.01(e).

(b) Employees and Representatives. Any natural person currently employed by CodeWeavers or acting in an official representative capacity on its behalf.

(c) Affiliated Entities. Any entity maintaining a formal affiliation, partnership, agency, or organizational relationship with CodeWeavers.

(d) Sponsored Persons. Any person or entity receiving sponsorship from CodeWeavers pursuant to an existing sponsorship agreement or arrangement.

(e) Endorsed Persons. Any person or entity that has knowingly accepted, adopted, or publicly represented an official endorsement by CodeWeavers.

(f) Agents and Contractors. Any person or entity acting pursuant to a contractual, agency, or representative relationship with CodeWeavers in connection with the Covered Materials.

(g) Circumvention Participants. Any person or entity knowingly participating in a Circumvention Arrangement.

Section 3.03. Prohibited Exercise of Rights

Excluded Persons shall have no authorization under this License to:

(a) Reproduce or distribute Covered Materials;

(b) Prepare or distribute Derivative Works of Covered Materials;

(c) Incorporate Covered Materials into commercial or noncommercial products;

(d) Sublicense or commercially exploit Covered Materials;

(e) Exercise Covered Rights through an intermediary, representative, contractor, or agent; or

(f) Otherwise engage in activities requiring authorization under copyright law where such authorization is purportedly derived from this License.

Section 3.04. Unsolicited Conduct

An unsolicited communication, unilateral request, public reference, or purported endorsement originating solely from CodeWeavers shall not, without acceptance or additional qualifying circumstances, establish that the recipient is an Excluded Person.

Section 3.05. Temporal Application

Excluded Person status shall be determined at the time the relevant Covered Right is exercised.

Termination of a qualifying relationship may restore eligibility for subsequent activities, subject to any outstanding violation or termination under Article IX.

ARTICLE IV. PROHIBITION AGAINST CIRCUMVENTION

Section 4.01. General Prohibition

No Licensee shall knowingly participate in, facilitate, or carry out a Circumvention Arrangement for the purpose of enabling an Excluded Person to obtain or exercise Covered Rights indirectly.

Section 4.02. Prohibited Arrangements

Without limiting Section 4.01, prohibited conduct includes:

(a) Reproducing or modifying Covered Materials pursuant to an arrangement undertaken on behalf of an Excluded Person;

(b) Procuring Covered Materials as an intermediary for an Excluded Person;

(c) Creating or maintaining Derivative Works pursuant to an arrangement intended to evade Article III;

(d) Transferring or sublicensing Covered Materials under an arrangement intended to confer prohibited rights upon an Excluded Person;

(e) Employing nominees, shell entities, contractors, agents, or other intermediaries to conceal an Excluded Person’s participation; and

(f) Knowingly assisting an Excluded Person in exercising rights withheld under this License through coordinated conduct.

Section 4.03. Requirement of Demonstrable Coordination

A violation of this Article requires knowing participation in an actual Circumvention Arrangement.

Mere speculation regarding an Excluded Person’s possible benefit shall not constitute sufficient grounds for establishing a violation.

Section 4.04. Independent Conduct

Nothing in this Article prohibits independent development, lawful research, public discussion, or activities undertaken without a Circumvention Arrangement.

