ARTICLE IX. TERMINATION AND REINSTATEMENT

Section 9.01. Automatic Termination

The rights granted to a Licensee under this License shall terminate automatically upon a material violation of its terms.

Section 9.02. Effect of Termination

Upon termination, the Licensee shall cease exercising all rights dependent upon this License.

Termination shall not affect rights independently granted under other applicable licenses.

Section 9.03. Cure and Reinstatement

Upon cessation of the violation, the Licensee’s rights shall be reinstated provisionally.

Reinstatement shall become permanent if:

(a) The relevant Licensor does not notify the Licensee of the violation within sixty (60) days following cessation; or

(b) The Licensee receives notice of the violation for the first time from the relevant Licensor and cures the violation within thirty (30) days after receiving such notice.

Section 9.04. Excluded Person Status

A person who becomes an Excluded Person shall cease to be eligible to exercise Covered Rights for the duration of such status.

The subsequent cessation of Excluded Person status shall not excuse violations occurring during the period of exclusion.

Section 9.05. Existing Compliant Grants

Termination shall not automatically terminate valid grants previously received by independent, compliant Licensees.

